{"schemaVersion":1,"id":"reference:eef80ab0afbe57c9","name":"Earphone Binary-to-Basic Translator","source":{"id":"source:reference-eef80ab0afbe57c9","title":"Earphone Binary-to-Basic Translator","revision":21032,"timestamp":"2024-08-26T01:01:58Z","sha256":"9eff5e12d2cab9e777e7dfc38316c84fb9ead89c60f2f34a53282114d85d5a61","url":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?oldid=21032","history":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?title=Earphone%20Binary-to-Basic%20Translator&action=history"},"article":{"sourceId":"source:reference-eef80ab0afbe57c9","blocks":[{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"i","children":["Reference Book: ",{"tag":"a","children":["Scavenger's Guide to Droids"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Scavenger%27s_Guide_to_Droids"}]},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":["Cost:"]}," 20\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":["Weight:"]}," 0.5 Kilograms\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Binary"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Binary","referenceId":"reference:ee1c8277caf5fb9b"}," is the primary language of ",{"tag":"a","children":["Droids"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Droids","referenceId":"reference:6e72e583603b9ea8"},". This ",{"tag":"a","children":["Translator Unit"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Translator_Unit","referenceId":"reference:0bcd4b383b11cac0"}," is installed on a Droid's Basic-output jack, a standard jack found on most ",{"tag":"a","children":["Droids"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Droids","referenceId":"reference:6e72e583603b9ea8"}," that enables them to connect to a terminal or a ",{"tag":"a","children":["Datapad"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Datapad","referenceId":"reference:7a32da74ac188805"}," and to express themselves in written Basic. The translator converts audible ",{"tag":"a","children":["Binary"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Binary","referenceId":"reference:ee1c8277caf5fb9b"}," into audible Basic, transmitting the spoken words to an earphone receiver. The less expensive version requires a large headphone set, while the more expensive version transmits to an earbud receiver. Detecting the earbud requires a ",{"tag":"a","children":["Perception"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Perception","referenceId":"reference:bd18e320a6bb9f53"}," check of DC 20.\n"]},"\n","\n","\n","\n\n","\n\n","\n"]}}
